# ============================================================
# Project         : IAM Privilege Escalation Lab
# Detection Name  : IAM Privilege Escalation - AdministratorAccess Attached
# Detection Type  : Elastic Security KQL Rule
# MITRE ATT&CK    : T1098 - Account Manipulation
# ATT&CK Tactics  : TA0004 (Privilege Escalation)
#                   TA0003 (Persistence)
# Severity        : High
# Platform        : AWS CloudTrail + Elastic Security
# Author          : Abhinav Maurya
# ============================================================

/*
Description
-----------
Detects when an IAM principal attaches the AWS managed
AdministratorAccess policy to an IAM user using the AttachUserPolicy API.

Rule Configuration
------------------
Index Pattern          : logs-*
Runs Every             : 1 minute
Additional Look-back   : 120 minutes
Severity               : High
Risk Score             : 80
*/

event.action:"AttachUserPolicy"
and aws.cloudtrail.flattened.request_parameters:*AdministratorAccess*

/*
Key Investigation Fields
------------------------
@timestamp
event.action
source.ip
user.name
aws.cloudtrail.user_identity.arn
aws.cloudtrail.user_identity.access_key_id
aws.cloudtrail.flattened.request_parameters
cloud.account.id

Response Guidance
-----------------
1. Identify who attached AdministratorAccess.
2. Identify the target IAM user.
3. Verify source IP and access key.
4. Confirm whether the action was authorized.
5. Detach the policy and rotate credentials if malicious.
*/